# Cloned upstream repos kept as read-only reference (~5 GB, each has its own .git) — ignored,
# but the upstream-URL + pinned-commit manifest IS tracked so the refs are reproducible.
reference/*
!reference/MANIFEST.md
# rubicon is NOT a cloned repo — it's small, curated, explorer-fetched verified source the
# 8x-01 docs depend on (provenance in its README + file headers). Tracked as an exception.
!reference/rubicon/

# The Zipcode UI lives in its own repo (resi-labs-ai/zipcode-finance-euler); this monorepo's
# frontend/ is a local dev scratch dir only, not part of the public repo.
frontend/

# subgraph/ is empty scaffolding, not yet real — kept local until there's something to publish.
subgraph/

# docs-site/ duplicates published docs living elsewhere — not part of this repo.
docs-site/

# Security work-in-progress: raw auditor reports, adversarial-review prompts/tooling, and
# generated build artifacts/tickets. Local only until findings are resolved and published
# via the external audit process.
audit/
adversarial-review/
build/

# Bridge work-in-progress: relocated auditor findings (verbatim exploit scenarios + fix diffs),
# third-party incident forensics, and the pre-mainnet requirements derived from them. Same
# never-publish rationale as the analysis reports above — an open-findings roadmap plus a live
# account of an incumbent's unremediated failure. Local only.
bridge/

# Foundry build artifacts
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/

# Local env / secrets (the .example template stays tracked)
.env
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example
contracts/.env

# NEVER-PUBLISH (this repo is PUBLIC).
# Raw auditor reports: unremediated findings + exploit scenarios + the fix diffs = an attack
# roadmap while the findings are still open. Triage/response lives in the audit workflow, not here.
resi-labs-ai-zipcode-euler-*-analysis.md
resi-labs-ai-zipcode-euler-*-analysis*.md
*-analysis.md
*-analysis (*).md

# Internal exit-design working notes (two-lane exit, fairness debate) — internal planning, not
# protocol documentation, and not a filename for a public repo. Lives in cre/ until the CRE review.
FUCK_UR_MOM.md

# Internal planning + strategy that is not protocol documentation. Matched by name at any
# depth — carry-risk names the still-open soft spots and points into the private crank trees,
# so it must not land in this repo no matter which directory it is dropped in.
fable.md
carry-risk.md
